From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Quick Options' filled controls take one quiet state fill (ADR-043)

Ink used as a fill is symmetric by design -- white on dark, near-black on
paper -- so in light mode Quick Options' on tiles, checked pills and slider
handles were heavy blocks, several to a panel. Four owner reports, measured:

  - On and off tiles looked the same because they were the same. luma-shelf.css
    gives the light icon plate #ffffff with one rule at the specificity of the
    variant sheet's :checked plate, and wins by order, so an on tile's plate
    measured 1.00:1 against an off tile's.
  - Slider handles were solid #3d444c dots in light, #f2f5f7 in glass.
  - A tile's chevron sat on its own white plate, which read as a hole cut in
    the tile.
  - Notifications and Calendar are plain St `button`s nobody styled, so they
    took the variant sheet's stock button: a dark slab whenever the dark sheet
    was loaded, which in light mode was always until 0152.

js/ui/lumaControlInk.js is the ledger for this, next to SURFACE_INK and with
the app kit's values, so a Quick Options toggle and an app's segment are the
same colour: one `state` slate with `stateInk` on it for every on state, a
`knob` disc ringed in `knobRing` for a handle, and the ledger's `ink`, `line`,
`control` and `hover` for the quiet controls. data/theme/luma-controls.css
spends it; shelf.js loads it after luma-shelf.css, and every selector is one
class more specific than the rule it replaces.

  mode   state    glyph on it   on vs off plate   before (on vs off)
  light  #61728a  4.90:1        4.90:1            1.00:1
  dark   #8a99a8  5.99:1        4.62:1            10.87:1 (white plate)
  frost  #a9b5c1  8.38:1        6.46:1            10.55:1 (white plate)
  glass  #a9b5c1  8.38:1        3.34:1            6.36:1  (#f2f5f7 plate)

Worst case over the panel veil and the raised veil, frost and glass over pure
white and pure black, shadow discounted. Chevrons and route buttons carry the
ledger ink at 8.95:1 or more on a tile, hovered included.

verify-treatment-ink.py grows three things:
  - a plate is any opaque fill the rule's own ink clears at 4.5:1, not only a
    near-white one: the state slate is mid-tone on purpose;
  - a filled-control pass that reads CONTROL_INK and SURFACE_INK from the
    modules themselves and fails if luma-controls.css spends a colour the
    ledger does not name for that mode, or if any pair above drops below 3:1
    (fills, rings) or 4.5:1 (glyphs, button ink); St slider rules, whose
    `color` is the handle fill, say so with an `ink-guard: handle` comment;
  - a notification pass: the island's Sass map must use the ledger's hover and
    press, and ink and muted ink must hold 4.5:1 on the card, the arriving
    surface and the tray, at rest, hovered, pressed, hover under hover and
    hover under press. That is the island on the Shelf and off it (the tray,
    a banner). A stale 0.22 press on frost now fails it at 4.40:1.

Touches none of 0151's, 0152's, 0153's or 0154's files. The gresource lines
are placed away from 0149's, so the queue can order them freely.

Verified from a patches-only tree: the 0148 tree, 0149 (screen-sharing-picker-r2
@9b3a9b44), 0150 @554e4109, then this; 0 rejects; verify-treatment-ink.py PASS.

Generated against the 0150 tree (shelf-ink-contract @554e4109); release at
build time.
